* large_source.sno -- regression for the dcftn brief
* "dcsno-source-byte-cap". Pre-fix, source files above
* SRC_LIMIT=12280 bytes silently truncated mid-line, corrupting
* parse output. After raising SRC_SIZE 12 KiB -> 64 KiB, sources
* up to ~64 KiB compile and run cleanly; only sources above the
* new cap trigger the "truncated at byte=" diagnostic.
*
* This file is ~20 KB: ~240 padding comment lines plus a
* trivial OUTPUT + END. Pre-fix, the file would never reach the
* OUTPUT statement -- truncation drops it. Post-fix, the file
* compiles fully and emits 'large source loaded'.
*
* padding comment line 1 -- keep the byte count above the old SRC_LIMIT=12280 cap
* padding comment line 2 -- keep the byte count above the old SRC_LIMIT=12280 cap
